# Line Endings (LF)

All text in this repo uses **LF** (`\n`). Never **CRLF** (`\r\n`).

Applies to code and config such as `.cpp`, `.h`, `.hpp`, `.c`, `.cc`, `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.js`, `.jsx`, `.json`, `.md`, `.yml`, `.yaml`, `.sh`, `.cmake`, `Makefile`, `.html`, `.gitattributes`, and similar text sources.

When creating or rewriting a file, write it with LF only. Do not introduce CRLF on Windows.

If git HEAD or the working tree already has CRLF, convert to LF anyway. Do not restore CRLF to match history, `git diff` cleanliness, or Windows checkout defaults. `.gitattributes` sets `eol=lf` for the whole repo.
